DEBUG: say where a missing file was looked for.

    tcc: error: file 'crt1.o' not found

That names the file and not one of the directories it was sought in. From the
outside, "the search path is wrong" and "the file really is absent" look
identical -- and they need opposite fixes. Several rounds of this spike went
into guessing which: reproducing the failure, reasoning about multiarch
triplets, changing configure flags, and re-reading the same log line unchanged
each time. The answer was in s->crt_paths throughout and the program simply
never printed it.

This prints every path that was tried, and calls out an EMPTY list separately,
because zero paths and a wrong path are indistinguishable in the current
message and mean different things: zero means the CONFIG_* macros expanded to
nothing, which is exactly what happened here -- -D TCC_TARGET_ARM64 on the
command line skipped the config.h block that defines CONFIG_TRIPLET, so
USE_TRIPLET(s) collapsed to s.

It is a tcc-debug patch: applied to the micro-c copy only, never to the
control, so the comparison stays honest.

diff --git a/libtcc.c b/libtcc.c
index 171e362..3800e7c 100644
--- a/libtcc.c
+++ b/libtcc.c
@@ -1266,9 +1266,30 @@ static int tcc_add_library_internal(TCCState *s1, const char *fmt,
         if (ret != FILE_NOT_FOUND)
             return ret;
     }
-    if (flags & AFF_PRINT_ERROR)
+    if (flags & AFF_PRINT_ERROR) {
         tcc_error_noabort("%s '%s' not found",
             flags & AFF_TYPE_LIB ? "library" : "file", filename);
+        /* SAY WHERE WE LOOKED.
+         *
+         * "file 'crt1.o' not found" names the file and not one of the
+         * directories it was sought in, so the log cannot distinguish "the
+         * path list is wrong" from "the file really is missing" -- and those
+         * need opposite fixes. Several rounds went into guessing which,
+         * reproducing the failure and theorising about triplets, when the
+         * program had the answer in s->crt_paths the whole time and simply
+         * never said it.
+         *
+         * An empty list is called out separately, because zero paths and a
+         * wrong path look identical from the outside and mean different
+         * things: zero means the CONFIG_* macros expanded to nothing. */
+        if (nb_paths == 0) {
+            fprintf(stderr, "        (no search paths at all -- the path"
+                            " macros expanded to nothing)\n");
+        } else {
+            for (i = 0; i < nb_paths; i++)
+                fprintf(stderr, "        looked in: %s\n", paths[i]);
+        }
+    }
     return FILE_NOT_FOUND;
 }
 
